# Prompt Templates

This folder documents the model-visible prompt composition used by LLMebots.
The complete rendered prompt artifacts are in the appendix prompt directory:
../additional/appendix_prompts/. Python implementation comments and
preprocessing details are intentionally omitted.

## Common WBT-generation messages

All WBT-generation strategies share this system message:

    You are an AI assistant that produces Webots simulator world files in the .wbt format. Output only the raw file content -- no markdown fences, no commentary.

The direct pipeline uses:

    Generate the .wbt content for the scene described below.

    Description: <scene_description>

The JSON-to-WBT stage uses:

    Generate the .wbt content for the scene described by the JSON spec below.

    Spec: <compiled_spec>

## Prompt composition

Let d be the natural-language description, j the intermediate JSON
specification, B the fixed structural-rule block, K(.) retrieved catalog
context, and E_NL/E_JSON the direct/JSON demonstration blocks.

| Strategy | Direct | JSON-to-WBT |
|---|---|---|
| S0 | T_NL(d) | T_JSON(j) |
| S1 | B + T_NL(d) | B + T_JSON(j) |
| S2 | B + K(d) + T_NL(d) | B + K(j) + T_JSON(j) |
| S3 | B + E_NL + T_NL(d) | B + E_JSON + T_JSON(j) |
| S4 | B + K(d) + E_NL + T_NL(d) | B + K(j) + E_JSON + T_JSON(j) |

S1--S4 use the same structural rules. Catalog context is scene-dependent;
the included catalog file is a representative held-out example. S3 and S4
use fixed demonstrations, with separate examples for natural-language and
JSON input.

## Artifact map

- `structural_rules_model_visible.txt`: rules after comment filtering;
- `retrieved_catalog_example.txt`: representative scene-dependent catalog context;
- `fewshot_direct_model_visible.txt`: direct-pipeline demonstrations;
- `fewshot_json_model_visible.txt`: JSON-to-WBT demonstrations;
- `compiler_user_template.txt` and `compiler_user_template_latex.txt`: natural-language-to-JSON compiler templates in plain-text and LaTeX-safe forms.
